From 651d4fff99d79d022101de65a306bfc89fd6297f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:57:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] semantic: recognize cc and c++ on Windows

MinGW toolchains ship cc.exe and c++.exe (GCC in MinGW-w64, Clang in
llvm-mingw), and make's default CC=cc runs them. The --version probe
that classifies these names was Unix-only, so on Windows they were never
recognized and bear -- make wrote an empty compilation database. The
probe now runs on Windows too (the child alone is killed on timeout, as
there is no process group), and .exe is dropped before the name is
looked up.
---
 .../compilers/compiler_recognition.rs         |   6 +
 .../src/interpreters/compilers/probe.rs       | 168 +++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 133 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/semantic/src/interpreters/compilers/compiler_recognition.rs b/crates/semantic/src/interpreters/compilers/compiler_recognition.rs
